# An allowlist: this repository is public, the texts it works from are not. Everything is ignored except code, docs, the
# licences and the few data files admitted below; anything new stays local until it is admitted here on purpose. The
# pre-commit hook (tools/screen.py) screens what is admitted.
*
!*/
!*.py
!*.sh
!*.md
!/LICENSE
!/LICENSE-docs
!/.gitignore
# lexeme-aligner, a core tool, as a git submodule at its pin (shared/pins.py); its .venv stays inside it, untracked
!/.gitmodules
!/.githooks/
!/.githooks/*
!/tools/screen_allow.txt
!/requirements.txt
!/requirements-nllb.txt
!/.github/
!/.github/workflows/
!/.github/workflows/*.yml
# the closed list: chapters and books held out of every evidence pool, training and measurement (no text)
!/shared/closed.json
# the register's shared questionnaire (questions only, no language's answers): register/README.md
!/register/parameters.tsv
# imported editions, filed by licence (import/README.md): an edition's description is tracked, its text never
!/import/_template/edition.yaml
!/import/*/*/*/edition.yaml

# never, even where a pattern above admits it
/private/
/internal-docs/
/external/*
!/external/lexeme-aligner
# an edition's subfolders (text/, source/) whatever they hold
/import/*/*/*/*/
/CLAUDE.local.md
/env.local.sh
__pycache__/
